":"zig-expert is a native Zig TypeScript runtime that provides expert guidance for writing idiomatic Zig code, following the Zen of Zig principles","zh":"zig-expert 是一个用于编写 idiomatic Zig 代码的工具，遵循 Zen of Zig 的核心哲学","ja":"zig-expert は、Zen of Zig のコア哲学に従って Idiomatic Zig コードを書くためのツールです","ko":"zig-expert는 Zen of Zig의 핵심 철학을 따르는 아이디어매틱 Zig 코드를 작성하기 위한 도구입니다","es":"zig-expert es un runtime nativo escrito en Zig que ejecuta TypeScript. Comenzó como un port del proyecto mquickjs y ahora proporciona orientación experta sobre los principios del Zen de Zig para una programación idiomática.","fr":"zig-expert est un runtime natif écrit en Zig exécutant TypeScript. Il a débuté comme un portage du projet mquickjs et offre désormais un guide expert sur les principes du Zen de Zig pour une programmation idiomatique.","de":"zig-expert ist eine in Zig geschriebene native Laufzeitumgebung für TypeScript. Sie begann als Port des mquickjs-Projekts und bietet nun Expertenanleitung zu den Prinzipien des Zen von Zig für idiomatische Programmierung.","pt":"O que é zig-expert? Um runtime de TypeScript nativo em Zig para desenvolvimento de código idiômático","ru":"Что такое ИИ Агент zig-expert? Родной среды выполнения TypeScript в Zig для написания идjomатичного кода","ar":"ما هو zig-expert? وقت تشغيل TypeScript أصلي في لغة Zig لتطوير код أصلية"},"features":{"en":["Provides expert guidance on idiomatic Zig programming","Emphasizes explicit intent and compile-time optimization","Follows the Zen of Zig principles for efficient code","Optimizes for reading over writing, reducing undefined behaviors","Supports edge case handling for robust code"],"zh":["提供 idiomatic Zig 编程指导","遵循 Zen of Zig 的核心哲学","支持 explicit intent 和 no hidden control flow","优化读取性能","处理 edge cases"],"ja":["Idiomatic Zig コーディングを指導","Zen of Zig のコア哲学に従う","explicit intent と no hidden control flow をサポート","読み取り性能を最適化","エッジケースを処理"],"ko":["아이디어매틱 Zig 프로그래밍을 위한 가이드 제공","Zen of Zig의 핵심 철학을 따름","explicit intent와 no hidden control flow 지원","읽기 성능 최적화","에지 케이스 처리"],"es":["Runtime nativo Zig para TypeScript, evolucionado desde un port de mquickjs","Enseña el principio Zen de Zig de ''comunicar la intención con precisión''","Promueve código explícito donde las APIs hacen obvios los requisitos","Enfatiza el manejo de casos extremos sin comportamientos indefinidos","Optimiza la legibilidad del código sobre la facilidad de escritura","Favorece la ejecución en tiempo de compilación sobre el tiempo de ejecución"],"fr":["Runtime natif Zig pour TypeScript, ayant évolué d''un portage de mquickjs","Enseigne le principe Zen de Zig de ''communiquer l''intention avec précision''","Promouvoir un code explicite où les APIs rendent les exigences évidentes","Met l''accent sur la gestion des cas limites sans comportements indéfinis","Optimise la lisibilité du code plutôt que la facilité d''écriture","Favorise l''exécution à la compilation plutôt qu''à l''exécution"],"de":["Native Zig-Laufzeitumgebung für TypeScript, entstanden aus einem Port von mquickjs","Vermittelt das Zen-von-Zig-Prinzip der ''präzisen Absichtskommunikation''","Fördert expliziten Code, in dem APIs Anforderungen offensichtlich machen","Betonung der Behandlung von Grenzfällen ohne undefinierte Verhaltensweisen","Optimiert die Code-Lesbarkeit über die Schreibbarkeit","Bevorzugt Kompilierzeit- über Laufzeitausführung"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de código idiômático em Zig","Foco em explicitar a intenção e evitar comportamentos indefinidos","Implementação de princípios de Zen de Zig","Otimização para leitura em vez de escrita","Tratamento de casos de bordo"],"ru":["Написание идjomатичного кода на Zig","Учет принципов явного намерения и отсутствия неопределенных поведений","Реализация принципов Zen of Zig","Оптимизация для чтения вместо записи","Обработка краевых случаев"],"ar":["تطوير код أصلية في لغة Zig","التركيز على توضيح النية وتجنب السلوكيات الغير محددة","تنفيذ مبادئ Zen of Zig","تحسين القراءة بدلاً من الكتابة","معالجة الحالات الحدودية"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use zig-expert","zig-expert alternative","zig-expert setup guide","what is zig-expert","zig-expert vs mquickjs","install zig-expert","idiomatic zig programming","zen of zig principles","zig typescript runtime"],"zh":["zig-expert","idiomatic Zig","Zen of Zig","explicit intent","no hidden control flow","读取性能优化","edge cases"],"ja":["zig-expert","Idiomatic Zig","Zen of Zig","explicit intent","no hidden control flow","読み取り性能最適化","エッジケース"],"ko":["zig-expert","아이디어매틱 Zig","Zen of Zig","explicit intent","no hidden control flow","읽기 성능 최적화","에지 케이스"],"es":["zig runtime typescript","programación zig idiomática","zen de zig","mquickjs port zig","aprendizaje zig AI Agent","código explícito zig","manejo casos extremos zig","compilación tiempo zig"],"fr":["runtime zig typescript","programmation zig idiomatique","zen de zig","portage mquickjs zig","apprentissage zig outil d''IA","code explicite zig","gestion cas limites zig","compilation zig"],"de":["zig runtime typescript","idiomatische zig programmierung","zen von zig","mquickjs port zig","zig lernen KI Agent","expliziter code zig","grenzfälle behandeln zig","kompilierzeit zig"],"pt":["zig-expert","desenvolvimento de código idiômático","Zig","TypeScript","runtime","desenvolvimento de software","programação","idiomatic code"],"ru":["ИИ Агент zig-expert","написание идjomатичного кода","Zig","TypeScript","среда выполнения","разработка программного обеспечения","программирование","идjomатичный код"],"ar":["zig-expert","تطوير код أصلية","لغة Zig","TypeScript","وقت تشغيل","تطوير البرمجيات","البرمجة","كود أصلية"]}},"owner":"srdjan","repo":"zigttp","repoPath":"srdjan/zigttp","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.425Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zig-expert","description":"Write idiomatic Zig code following the Zen of Zig philosophy. Use for systems programming with Zig (.zig files), covering manual memory management with allocators, error unions and explicit error handling, compile-time programming (comptime), data-oriented design, and the new async/Io model. Applies functional programming parallels (Result types, ADTs, explicit effects) for C-free systems development.","bodyPreview":"# Idiomatic Zig Programming\n\nExpert guidance for writing idiomatic Zig code that embodies the Zen of Zig: explicit intent, no hidden control flow, and compile-time over runtime.\n\n## Zen of Zig (Core Philosophy)\n\nThese principles govern all idiomatic Zig code:\n\n| Principle | Implication |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Communicate intent precisely | Explicit code; APIs make requirements obvious |\n| Edge cases matter | No undefined behaviors glossed over |\n| Favor reading over writing | Optimize fo","body":"# Idiomatic Zig Programming\n\nExpert guidance for writing idiomatic Zig code that embodies the Zen of Zig: explicit intent, no hidden control flow, and compile-time over runtime.\n\n## Zen of Zig (Core Philosophy)\n\nThese principles govern all idiomatic Zig code:\n\n| Principle | Implication |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Communicate intent precisely | Explicit code; APIs make requirements obvious |\n| Edge cases matter | No undefined behaviors glossed over |\n| Favor reading over writing | Optimize for clarity and maintainability |\n| One obvious way | Avoid multiple complex features for same task |\n| Runtime crashes > bugs | Fail fast and loudly, never corrupt state silently |\n| Compile errors > runtime crashes | Catch issues at compile-time when possible |\n| Resource deallocation must succeed | Design APIs with allocation failure in mind |\n| Memory is a resource | Manage memory as consciously as any other resource |\n| No hidden control flow | No exceptions, no GC, no implicit allocations |\n\n## FP Conceptual Parallels\n\nZig shares key concepts with functional programming:\n\n| FP Concept | Zig Equivalent |\n|------------|----------------|\n| Result/Either type | Error union `!T` (either error or value) |\n| Option/Maybe | Optional `?T` (nullable type) |\n| ADTs / Sum types | Tagged unions with `union(enum)` |\n| Pattern matching | `switch` with exhaustive handling |\n| Explicit effects | Allocator/Io parameters (dependency injection) |\n| Immutability preference | `const` by default, `var` only when needed |\n| Pure functions | Functions without hidden state or allocations |\n\n## Workflow Decision Tree\n\n1. **Declaring a binding?** → Use `const` unless mutation required\n2. **Function needs memory?** → Accept `Allocator` parameter, never global alloc\n3. **Function can fail?** → Return error union `!T`, use `try` to propagate\n4. **Handling an error?** → Use `catch` with explicit handler or `try` to propagate\n5. **Need cleanup on exit?** → Use `defer` immediately after acquisition\n6. **Cleanup only on error?** → Use `errdefer` for conditional cleanup\n7. **Need generic code?** → Use `comptime` type parameters\n8. **Compile-time known value?** → Use `comptime` to evaluate at build time\n9. **Calling C code?** → Use `@cImport` for seamless FFI\n10. **Need async I/O?** → Pass `Io` interface, use `io.async()` and `future.await()`\n11. **Optimizing hot path?** → Consider data-oriented design (SoA vs AoS)\n\n## Essential Patterns\n\n### Error Unions (Result Type Equivalent)\n\n```zig\nconst FileError = error{ NotFound, PermissionDenied, InvalidPath };\n\nfn readConfig(path: []const u8) FileError!Config {\n    const file = std.fs.cwd().openFile(path, .{}) catch |err| {\n        return switch (err) {\n            error.FileNotFound => error.NotFound,\n            error.AccessDenied => error.PermissionDenied,\n            else => error.InvalidPath,\n        };\n    };\n    defer file.close();\n    // ... parse config\n    return config;\n}\n\n// Propagate with try (like Rust''s ?)\npub fn main() !void {\n    const config = try readConfig(\"app.conf\");\n    // ...\n}\n\n// Handle explicitly with catch\npub fn mainSafe() void {\n    const config = readConfig(\"app.conf\") catch |err| {\n        std.debug.print(\"Failed: {}\\n\", .{err});\n        return;\n    };\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Allocator Pattern (Explicit Effects)\n\n```zig\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\n\n// Function signature communicates: \"I need to allocate\"\nfn processData(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, input: []const u8) ![]u8 {\n    var result = try allocator.alloc(u8, input.len * 2);\n    errdefer allocator.free(result); // cleanup only on error path\n    \n    // ... process into result\n    \n    return result; // caller owns this memory\n}\n\npub fn main() !void {\n    var gpa = std.heap.GeneralPurposeAllocator(.{}){};\n    defer _ = gpa.deinit();\n    const allocator = gpa.allocator();\n    \n    const data = try processData(allocator, \"input\");\n    defer allocator.free(data); // caller responsible for cleanup\n}\n```\n\n### Tagged Unions (ADTs / Sum Types)\n\n```zig\nconst PaymentState = union(enum) {\n    pending: void,\n    processing: struct { transaction_id: []const u8 },\n    completed: Receipt,\n    failed: PaymentError,\n    \n    // Methods on the union\n    pub fn describe(self: PaymentState) []const u8 {\n        return switch (self) {\n            .pending => \"Waiting for payment\",\n            .processing => |p| p.transaction_id,\n            .completed => |r| r.summary,\n            .failed => |e| e.message,\n        };\n    }\n};\n\n// Exhaustive switch (compiler enforces all cases)\nfn handlePayment(state: PaymentState) void {\n    switch (state) {\n        .pending => startProcessing(),\n        .processing => |p| pollStatus(p.transaction_id),\n        .completed => |receipt| sendConfirmation(receipt),\n        .failed => |err| notifyFailure(err),\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Compile-Time Programming\n\n```zig\n// comptime function for generics\nfn max(comptime T: type, a: T, b: T) T {\n    return if (a > b) a else b;\n}\n\n// Compile-time computed constants\nconst LOOKUP_TABLE = blk: {\n    var table: [256]u8 = undefined;\n    for (&table, 0..) |*entry, i| {\n        entry.* = @intCast((i * 7) % 256);\n    }\n    break :blk table;\n};\n\n// Generic container (like TypeScript generics)\nfn ArrayList(comptime T: type) type {\n    return struct {\n        items: []T,\n        allocator: std.mem.Allocator,\n        \n        const Self = @This();\n        \n        pub fn init(allocator: std.mem.Allocator) Self {\n            return .{ .items = &[_]T{}, .allocator = allocator };\n        }\n        \n        pub fn append(self: *Self, item: T) !void {\n            // ...\n        }\n    };\n}\n```\n\n### Resource Management with defer\n\n```zig\nfn processFile(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, path: []const u8) !void {\n    // Open file\n    const file = try std.fs.cwd().openFile(path, .{});\n    defer file.close(); // ALWAYS runs on scope exit\n    \n    // Allocate buffer\n    const buffer = try allocator.alloc(u8, 4096);\n    defer allocator.free(buffer); // cleanup guaranteed\n    \n    // errdefer for conditional cleanup\n    var result = try allocator.alloc(u8, 1024);\n    errdefer allocator.free(result); // only on error\n    \n    // If we reach here successfully, caller owns result\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```zig\n// Imports\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\n\n// Variables\nconst immutable: u32 = 42;        // prefer const\nvar mutable: u32 = 0;             // only when needed\n\n// Optionals (?T) - like Option/Maybe\nvar maybe_value: ?u32 = null;\nconst unwrapped = maybe_value orelse 0;        // default value\nconst ptr = maybe_value orelse return error.Missing;  // early return\n\n// Error unions (!T) - like Result/Either\nfn canFail() !u32 { return error.SomeError; }\nconst value = try canFail();                   // propagate error\nconst safe = canFail() catch |err| handleError(err);  // catch error\n\n// Slices (pointer + length, not null-terminated)\nconst slice: []const u8 = \"hello\";             // string literal is []const u8\nconst arr: [5]u8 = .{ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };\nconst sub = arr[1..3];                         // slice of array\n\n// Iteration\nfor (slice, 0..) |byte, index| { }             // value and index\nfor (slice) |byte| { }                         // value only\n\n// Switch (exhaustive, can capture)\nswitch (tagged_union) {\n    .variant => |captured| doSomething(captured),\n    else => {},  // or handle all cases\n}\n\n// Comptime\nconst SIZE = comptime blk: { break :blk 64; };\nfn generic(comptime T: type, val: T) T { return val; }\n```\n\n## Detailed References\n\n- **[references/idioms.md](references/idioms.md)** - Data-oriented design, memory patterns, testing\n- **[references/async-io.md](references/async-io.md)** - New async/Io model, futures, cancellation\n- **[references/c-interop.md](references/c-interop.md)** - C FFI, @cImport, ABI compatibility\n\n## Forbidden Patterns\n\n| ❌ Never | ✅ Instead |\n|----------|-----------|\n| Global allocator / hidden malloc | Pass `Allocator` explicitly |\n| Exceptions / panic for errors | Return error union `!T` |\n| Null pointers without type | Use optional `?*T` |\n| Preprocessor macros | Use `comptime` and inline functions |\n| C-style strings in Zig code | Use slices `[]const u8` |\n| Ignoring errors silently | Handle with `catch` or propagate with `try` |\n| `var` when `const` works | Default to `const`, mutate only when necessary |\n| Hidden control flow | Make all branches explicit |\n| OOP inheritance hierarchies | Use composition and tagged unions |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:07:28.117Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing expertise in idiomatic Zig programming with explicit intent and compile-time optimization.","zh":"非常适合需要掌握习惯用Zig编程、显式意图和编译时优化的代码生成代理。","ja":"Zigプログラミングのイディオムと明示的な意図、コンパイル時の最適化に精通するコード生成エージェントに最適です。","ko":"자연스러운 Zig 프로그래밍, 명시적 의도 및 컴파일 타임 최적화에 전문성이 필요한 코드 생성 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Generación de Código que necesitan experiencia en programación idiomática Zig con intención explícita y optimización en tiempo de compilación.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Génération de Code ayant besoin d''expertise en programmation idiomatique Zig avec intention explicite et optimisation à temps de compilation.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Generation-Agenten, die Erfahrung in idiomatischer Zig-Programmierung mit expliziter Absicht und Kompilierzeitoptimierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Geração de Código que precisam de expertise em programação Zig idiomática com intenção explícita e otimização em tempo de compilação.","ru":"Идеально для агентов генерации кода, которым необходимы знания в области идиоматического программирования на Zig с явным намерением и оптимизацией во время компиляции.","ar":"مثالي لعميل توليد الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى الخبرة في برمجة Zig القائمة على الاصطلاحات مع النية الصريحة وتحسين وقت الترجمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write efficient Zig code embodying the Zen of Zig principles, leveraging compile-time evaluation and explicit control flow to optimize performance, and utilizing APIs that make requirements obvious.","zh":"赋予代理编写高效的Zig代码的能力，体现Zig的禅宗原则，利用编译时评估和显式控制流来优化性能，并使用使要求明显的API。","ja":"コンパイル時の評価と明示的な制御フローを使用してパフォーマンスを最適化し、要件を明らかにするAPIを使用して、効率的なZigコードをエージェントが記述できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 효율적인 Zig 코드를 작성할 수 있도록 해주는 기능을 제공하여, Zig의 정취를 구현하고 컴파일 타임 평가 및 명시적 제어 흐름을 사용하여 성능을 최적화하고 요구 사항을 명확하게 하는 API를 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir código Zig eficiente que encarna los principios del Zen de Zig, aprovechando la evaluación en tiempo de compilación y el control de flujo explícito para optimizar el rendimiento, y utilizando APIs que hacen que los requisitos sean obvios.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire du code Zig efficace incarnant les principes du Zen de Zig, en exploitant l''évaluation à temps de compilation et le contrôle de flux explicite pour optimiser les performances, et en utilisant des API qui rendent les exigences évidentes.","de":"Ermöglich es den Agenten, effizienten Zig-Code zu schreiben, der die Prinzipien des Zen von Zig verkörpert, indem es die Kompilierzeitbewertung und den expliziten Kontrollfluss nutzt, um die Leistung zu optimieren, und APIs verwendet, die die Anforderungen offensichtlich machen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever código Zig eficiente que incorpora os princípios do Zen de Zig, aproveitando a avaliação em tempo de compilação e o controle de fluxo explícito para otimizar o desempenho, e utilizando APIs que tornam os requisitos óbvios.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать эффективный код на Zig, воплощающий принципы Zen of Zig, используя оценку во время компиляции и явный контроль потока для оптимизации производительности, а также использует API, которые делают требования очевидными.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من كتابة شفرة Zig فعالة تتمثل مبدأيات زين من Zig، من خلال الاستفادة من التقييم في وقت الترجمة والسيطرة الصريحة على تدفق التنفيذ لتحسين الأداء، واستخدام واجهات برمجة التطبيقات التي تجعل المتطلبات واضحة."},"useCases":{"en":["Writing high-performance Zig applications with minimal runtime overhead","Optimizing Zig code for embedded systems with strict resource constraints","Generating idiomatic Zig code snippets for developer tutorials and documentation"],"zh":["编写具有最小运行时开销的高性能Zig应用程序","针对严格资源约束的嵌入式系统优化Zig代码","为开发者教程和文档生成习惯用Zig代码片段"],"ja":["最小のランタイムオーバーヘッドを持つ高パフォーマンスのZigアプリケーションを記述する","厳格なリソース制約を持つ組み込みシステム向けにZigコードを最適化する","開発者向けチュートリアルやドキュメント用のイディオムなZigコードスニペットを生成する"],"ko":["최소한의 런타임 오버헤드가 있는 고성능 Zig 애플리케이션을 작성하는 것","严格한 자원 제약이 있는 내장형 시스템을 위한 Zig 코드 최적화","개발자 튜토리얼 및 문서를 위한 자연스러운 Zig 코드 조각 생성"],"es":["Escritura de aplicaciones Zig de alto rendimiento con un mínimo de sobrecarga en tiempo de ejecución","Optimización de código Zig para sistemas embebidos con estrictas limitaciones de recursos","Generación de fragmentos de código Zig idiomáticos para tutoriales y documentación de desarrolladores"],"fr":["Écriture d''applications Zig à haute performance avec une charge minimale en temps d''exécution","Optimisation de code Zig pour les systèmes embarqués avec des contraintes de ressources strictes","Génération de fragments de code Zig idiomatiques pour les didacticiels et la documentation des développeurs"],"de":["Schreiben von Zig-Anwendungen mit hoher Leistung und minimaler Laufzeitüberhead","Optimierung von Zig-Code für eingebettete Systeme mit strengen Ressourcenbeschränkungen","Generierung von idiomatischen Zig-Code-Snippets für Entwickler-Tutorials und -Dokumentationen"],"pt":["Escrever aplicações Zig de alto desempenho com sobrecarga de tempo de execução mínima","Otimizar código Zig para sistemas incorporados com restrições de recursos estritas","Gerar trechos de código Zig idiomáticos para tutoriais e documentação de desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Написание высокопроизводительных приложений на Zig с минимальной нагрузкой во время выполнения","Оптимизация кода на Zig для встроенных систем с жесткими ограничениями ресурсов","Генерация идиоматических фрагментов кода на Zig для уроков и документации разработчиков"],"ar":["كتابة تطبيقات Zig عالية الأداء مع تأثير زمن تشغيل أدنى","تحسين شفرة Zig لأنظمة متحركة ذات قيود موارد صارمة","توليد شفرة Zig قائم على الاصطلاحات لبرامج تعليمية وتوثيق المطورين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Zig programming language fundamentals","Focused on idiomatic Zig coding principles, may not support non-standard or obsolete Zig features"],"zh":["需要了解Zig编程语言的基本知识","专注于习惯用Zig编码原则，可能不支持非标准或过时的Zig功能"],"ja":["Zigプログラミング言語の基礎知識が必要","イディオムなZigコーディング原則に焦点を当てているため、非標準または古いZig機能はサポートされない可能性がある"],"ko":["Zig 프로그래밍 언어의 기본 지식이 필요","자연스러운 Zig 코딩 원칙에 중점을 두고 있으므로 비표준 또는 구식 Zig 기능은 지원되지 않을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de los fundamentos del lenguaje de programación Zig","Centrado en principios de codificación idiomáticos Zig, puede que no admita características no estándar u obsoletas de Zig"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des fondements du langage de programmation Zig","Axé sur les principes de codage idiomatiques Zig, peut ne pas supporter les fonctionnalités non standard ou obsolètes de Zig"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Grundlagen der Zig-Programmiersprache","Konzentriert sich auf idiomatische Zig-Coding-Prinzipien, unterstützt möglicherweise keine nicht standardmäßigen oder veralteten Zig-Features"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento dos fundamentos da linguagem de programação Zig","Focado em princípios de codificação Zig idiomáticos, pode não suportar recursos não padrão ou obsoletos do Zig"],"ru":["Требует знания основ языка программирования Zig","Фокусируется на идиоматических принципах кодирования на Zig, может не поддерживать нестандартные или устаревшие функции Zig"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة أساسيات لغة برمجة Zig","يركز على مبدأيات برمجة Zig القائمة على الاصطلاحات، وقد لا يدعم ميزات غير قياسية أو مُتقادمة من Zig"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"4e95bdb4fad789a04c1ea79dcb63ba5dcc0a679fcaff867d959346a2b89f1d44","qualityScore":39}');
